      "updated": 1786209720140,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "STRATEGY : \n1. I think there is no need to traverse the subRoot\n, what we will do by traversing subRoot ? \n\n2. Question is how to find the root of subRoot in\ntree 1 \n\n3. What if we compare values from bottom to up\n? \n\n4 .Fully traverse to left of both nodes , if left\ntraveresed value is similar to subroot left , move\nto the right and then check further",
      "fontSize": 16,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "STRATEGY : \n1. I think there is no need to traverse the subRoot , what we will do by traversing subRoot ? \n\n2. Question is how to find the root of subRoot in tree 1 \n\n3. What if we compare values from bottom to up ? \n\n4 .Fully traverse to left of both nodes , if left traveresed value is similar to subroot left , move to the right and then check further",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.35
    },
